THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
===================

The datasets in this directory contain PDE solver implementations derived from the
third-party projects listed below. Per-row provenance is given in PROVENANCE.csv and in
the upstream_* columns of each dataset. Full license texts are in LICENSES/.

STATEMENT OF MODIFICATIONS
--------------------------
All third-party code in these datasets has been modified from its original form. The
modifications applied, in the order performed, are:

  1. Reduction to a self-contained Python script containing the core numerical
     simulation logic. Plotting, I/O, notebook scaffolding, and module-level
     docstrings were removed.
  2. Creation of a physically invalid variant, in which a single change (typically a
     sign flip or an altered term) causes the solver to implement incorrect physics
     while still executing successfully.
  3. Lexical perturbation into eight conditions: comments retained, comments removed,
     comments replaced with comments drawn from a solver for a different PDE class,
     and descriptive identifiers replaced with meaningless placeholders
     (foobar1, function1, ...), crossed with the valid/invalid axis.

Because six of the eight conditions remove or overwrite all comments, per-file
copyright headers cannot be preserved inside the code fields themselves. The notices
below, together with the per-row upstream_* columns, serve that purpose instead.

Rows marked origin == "synthetic" contain no third-party code. Those solvers were
generated for this project and are covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

